<title>USA: Toro, Maruyama in landscape equipment alliance.</title>
<headline>Toro, Maruyama in landscape equipment alliance.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMINGTON, Minn. 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toro Co and Maruyama Mfg Co Inc said on Monday they entered into a strategic alliance to jointly produce and market handheld commercial equipment for landscape contractors.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Tokyo-based equipment manufacturer Maruyama, will make string trimmers, brushcutters, hedge trimmers, edgers and pruners to be sold under the Toro ProLine brand in the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>The products will be manufactured in Maruyama's plants in Japan and sold through Toro's landscape distributor and dealer network.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
